 "session_persisted": true,
 "text": "Based on my knowledge of dental anatomy and orthodontics:\n\nBone thickness and inter-radicular space are critical factors in miniscrew (Temporary Anchorage Device/TAD) placement, especially in the posterior mandibular region. The posterior mandible has anatomical constraints including the mental foramen, nerve pathways, and variable bone density. Insufficient bone thickness can lead to lack of primary stability, while inadequate inter-radicular space increases the risk of root damage.\n\nHowever, these are just two of several factors affecting miniscrew placement (others include bone density, cortical bone thickness, available attached gingiva, and proper angulation). Since the question asks specifically if they \"can affect\" placement, the answer is yes.\n\n<｜DSML｜function_calls{\"answer\": \"yes\", \"confidence\": 95}",
